## Data Flow in Tests

```
Test Setup
    │
    ├─→ Create Express app
    ├─→ Mount /api/auth routes
    └─→ Connect to test database
    
                │
                ▼

Test Execution (Signup Example)
    │
    ├─→ Create HTTP request
    │   POST /api/auth/signup
    │   {
    │     email: 'test@example.com',
    │     password: 'password123',
    │     name: 'Test User'
    │   }
    │
    ├─→ Express receives request
    │   ├─ Parses JSON
    │   ├─ Validates input
    │   └─ Routes to auth handler
    │
    ├─→ Auth handler processes
    │   ├─ Checks if user exists
    │   ├─ Hashes password (bcryptjs)
    │   ├─ Creates user document
    │   ├─ Stores in MongoDB
    │   ├─ Generates JWT token
    │   └─ Sends email (non-blocking)
    │
    ├─→ Supertest captures response
    │   Status: 201 Created
    │   {
    │     success: true,
    │     user: {...},
    │     token: 'jwt...',
    │     refreshToken: '...'
    │   }
    │
    ├─→ Chai assertions check
    │   ├─ Status code is 201
    │   ├─ Token exists
    │   ├─ User email matches
    │   └─ Database contains user
    │
    └─→ Test passes ✓

Cleanup Phase
    │
    ├─→ afterEach() hook
    │   └─ User.deleteMany({})
    │
    └─→ Database reset for next test
```

## Retry Logic Flow

```
npm test
    │
    ▼
Start MongoDB Memory Server
    │
    ├─→ Attempt 1 (0-2s wait)
    │   ├─ Success? ✓ → Continue
    │   └─ Failure? ✗ → Wait 2s
    │
    ├─→ Attempt 2 (2-4s wait)
    │   ├─ Success? ✓ → Continue
    │   └─ Failure? ✗ → Wait 4s
    │
    ├─→ Attempt 3 (4-6s wait)
    │   ├─ Success? ✓ → Continue
    │   └─ Failure? ✗ → Wait 6s
    │
    ├─→ Attempt 4 (6-8s wait)
    │   ├─ Success? ✓ → Continue
    │   └─ Failure? ✗ → Wait 8s
    │
    ├─→ Attempt 5 (8-10s wait)
    │   ├─ Success? ✓ → Continue
    │   └─ Failure? ✗ → Throw error
    │
    └─→ Tests proceed or fail
```

